214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (For hundreds of years, guar gum, a hard, drought-resistant legume crop, has been used to increase the resiliency and texture of baked goods, thicken dairy products, as a binding agent. It is an additive in salad dressings, ketchups, dry and frozen soups, instant foods and desserts. With a variety of pure and derivative grades, the free flowing guar powder offers several industrial applications as well.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
